# row-zero-differs.rq — does row 0 of a region differ from the body of its column?
# Box-split spec 2026-09-28 § 10.3.2 (the one-way oracle). Asked by rowzero.row_zero_differs over
# ONE region's transient evidence graph: celltype.grid_evidence's typed cells plus the three style
# facts rowzero.cell_styles extracts (tab:cellGlyphFont, tab:cellGlyphFill, tab:cellRectFill).
#
# TRUE iff a WITNESS exists: a column ?c and a feature f such that
#   1. the row-0 cell of ?c has a value ?v of f;
#   2. ?c has at least one body cell with a value of f;
#   3. no body cell of ?c has ?v.
# One UNION branch per feature. Each branch restates its own ?s / ?h / ?c bindings rather than
# sharing them with the others, because a UNION operand is a group evaluated on its own: a
# binding made outside it would not reach its FILTERs (the scoping looks-transposed.rq records).
#
# The features:
#   - the datatype FAMILY (tab:inDatatypeFamily; a datatype with no family is its own), with
#     abstaining datatypes (tab:datatypeAbstains — Blank, ParenthesizedNumber, UnshownInk) giving
#     no value on either side;
#   - glyph font name; glyph fill colour; the colour of each filled rect containing the cell's
#     centre. These three are compared as the literals rowzero.colour_literal spells, by RDF term
#     identity (a bound ?v in a triple pattern), so equality is exact.
#
# ROW 0 and BODY are read from the evidence, not written here: the head is the rows before
# tab:bodyStartsAt, the body the rows at or after it. rowzero passes grid_evidence's default
# split, so the head is exactly row 0. This keeps the query free of numeric literals (I-10-4).
#
# AXIOM, open-world derivation (CLAUDE.md § 8): a witness is a PRESENT value, so the query is
# evidence-positive. Its NOT EXISTS closes only within this one region's evidence graph — the
# holon-scoped closure. ONE-WAY: TRUE refutes "row 0 is data"; FALSE refutes nothing. A region
# with no body row never meets condition 2, and a header typed and styled as its body is silent.
PREFIX tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#>
ASK {
  {
    # --- the datatype family ---
    ?band tab:bodyStartsAt ?s .
    ?h tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?hr ; tab:cellDatatype ?hraw .
    FILTER(?hr < ?s)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?hraw tab:datatypeAbstains true }
    OPTIONAL { ?hraw tab:inDatatypeFamily ?hfam }
    BIND(COALESCE(?hfam, ?hraw) AS ?v)
    FILTER EXISTS {
      ?b tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?br ; tab:cellDatatype ?braw .
      FILTER(?br >= ?s)
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?braw tab:datatypeAbstains true }
    }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?n tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?nr ; tab:cellDatatype ?nraw .
      FILTER(?nr >= ?s)
      OPTIONAL { ?nraw tab:inDatatypeFamily ?nfam }
      FILTER(sameTerm(COALESCE(?nfam, ?nraw), ?v))
    }
  }
  UNION
  {
    # --- the glyph font ---
    ?band tab:bodyStartsAt ?s .
    ?h tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?hr ; tab:cellGlyphFont ?v .
    FILTER(?hr < ?s)
    FILTER EXISTS {
      ?b tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?br ; tab:cellGlyphFont ?any .
      FILTER(?br >= ?s)
    }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?n tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?nr ; tab:cellGlyphFont ?v .
      FILTER(?nr >= ?s)
    }
  }
  UNION
  {
    # --- the glyph fill ---
    ?band tab:bodyStartsAt ?s .
    ?h tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?hr ; tab:cellGlyphFill ?v .
    FILTER(?hr < ?s)
    FILTER EXISTS {
      ?b tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?br ; tab:cellGlyphFill ?any .
      FILTER(?br >= ?s)
    }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?n tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?nr ; tab:cellGlyphFill ?v .
      FILTER(?nr >= ?s)
    }
  }
  UNION
  {
    # --- the rect fill ---
    ?band tab:bodyStartsAt ?s .
    ?h tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?hr ; tab:cellRectFill ?v .
    FILTER(?hr < ?s)
    FILTER EXISTS {
      ?b tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?br ; tab:cellRectFill ?any .
      FILTER(?br >= ?s)
    }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?n tab:atGridColumn ?c ; tab:atGridRow ?nr ; tab:cellRectFill ?v .
      FILTER(?nr >= ?s)
    }
  }
}
